      "name": "GetNotificationValue",
      "signature": "uint GetNotificationValue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Simple getter function that retrieves notification value from global storage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the 32-bit notification value from global variable g_dwNotificationValue at address 0x6ff3962c\n2. Store the loaded value in EAX register for return to caller\n3. Execute RET instruction to return control to calling function\n\nParameters:\nvoid - No parameters required. Function operates entirely on global state.\n\nReturns:\nuint - Current notification value (32-bit unsigned integer)\n       Value represents the current state stored in g_dwNotificationValue global variable\n       Valid range: 0x00000000 to 0xFFFFFFFF (full 32-bit unsigned range)\n       Zero indicates default/uninitialized state\n\nSpecial Cases:\nGlobal Dependencies: Function has read-only dependency on g_dwNotificationValue global variable\nMemory Access: Single memory read operation at address 0x6ff3962c\nThread Safety: Function is inherently thread-safe (performs only atomic read operation)\nPerformance: Extremely fast operation - single MOV instruction followed by RET",
