      "name": "GetPacketHandler",
      "signature": "dword GetPacketHandler(dword bMessageId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves packet handler function pointer from global handler table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Mask message ID to byte range (0x00-0xFF) using bitwise AND\n2. Use masked ID as index into global packet handler function pointer array\n3. Return function pointer from array at calculated index\n\nParameters:\nbMessageId - Packet message type identifier (masked to 0x00-0xFF range)\n\nReturns:\nFunction pointer to packet handler for the specified message ID\nNULL (0) if no handler is registered for the message ID\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Message IDs > 255 are masked to byte range using AND 0xFF operation\n- Unregistered message IDs return NULL function pointer (array initialized to zero)\n- Array index bounds are guaranteed safe due to 0xFF mask limiting range to 0-255\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFF (255) - Byte mask to limit message ID to valid array index range (0-255)\n0x4 (4) - DWORD size multiplier for array indexing (ECX*4 addressing mode)\n0x6ff3951c - Base address of global packet handler function pointer array\n\nStructure Layout:\nPacketHandlerArray (1024 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type     | Description  \n0x000  | 4    | Handler0   | dword    | Function pointer for message ID 0x00\n0x004  | 4    | Handler1   | dword    | Function pointer for message ID 0x01\n...    | 4    | ...        | dword    | Function pointers for message IDs 0x02-0xFE\n0x3FC  | 4    | Handler255 | dword    | Function pointer for message ID 0xFF",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
