      "name": "InitializeNetworkBuffer",
      "signature": "int InitializeNetworkBuffer(int nBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initialize network buffer using STORM.DLL memory operation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call STORM.DLL Ordinal_501 with network buffer address (0x6ff397e8)\n2. Pass caller-provided buffer size parameter as second argument  \n3. Pass maximum size limit (0x7fffffff) as third argument\n4. Return success status (always returns 1)\n\nParameters:\nnBufferSize (int): Buffer size parameter passed to STORM.DLL function\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function always succeeds regardless of input parameters\n- Buffer address 0x6ff397e8 is fixed global network buffer\n- Maximum size 0x7fffffff (2,147,483,647) ensures no size overflow\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x6ff397e8 - Global network buffer address (first argument to Ordinal_501)\n0x7fffffff - Maximum size limit (2,147,483,647 bytes, third argument)\n0x1 - Success return code (loaded into EAX before return)",
