      "signature": "void CopyDataToGlobalBuffer(byte * pSourceData, uint dwDataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Copies data from source buffer to a global buffer using optimized memory transfer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global buffer is already allocated at offset 0x380\n2. If allocated, call cleanup function (Ordinal_10043) with parameters 0x3d6, 0\n3. Clear 4 bytes at global buffer offsets 0x17c-0x17f (set to zero)\n4. Allocate new buffer space using Ordinal_10042 with size 0x3e4 (996 bytes)\n5. Store allocated buffer pointer at global buffer offset 0x380\n6. Copy data in two phases for optimization:\n   - Phase 1: Copy data in 4-byte (DWORD) chunks using MOVSD.REP\n   - Phase 2: Copy remaining bytes (0-3 bytes) individually using MOVSB.REP\n7. Update source and destination pointers after each copy operation\n\nParameters:\n- pSourceData (byte*): Pointer to source buffer containing data to copy\n- dwDataSize (uint): Size of data to copy in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwDataSize is 0, no data is copied but buffer is still allocated\n- Handles unaligned data sizes efficiently by copying remainder bytes\n- Global buffer allocation size is fixed at 0x3e4 (996) bytes regardless of dwDataSize\n- Function assumes dwDataSize <= 996 bytes (no bounds checking performed)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x17c (380): Start offset in global buffer for clearing (4 bytes cleared)\n- 0x380 (896): Offset in global buffer where allocated pointer is stored\n- 0x3d6 (982): Parameter passed to cleanup function (Ordinal_10043)\n- 0x3e4 (996): Fixed allocation size for buffer (Ordinal_10042)\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking for allocation failure\n- No bounds checking for source data size vs allocation size\n- Assumes successful allocation from Ordinal_10042",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:661ecb5e140955c0a623d2153f720289",
