      "name": "ReallocateGlobalBuffer",
      "signature": "void ReallocateGlobalBuffer(byte * pbSourceBuffer, uint dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Reallocates the global buffer with new data and size.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global buffer already exists (g_pGlobalBuffer != 0)\n2. If existing buffer present, call Ordinal_10043(0x4ac, 0) to free it\n3. Call Ordinal_10042(0x4ad, 0) to allocate new buffer with specified size\n4. Store new buffer pointer in g_pGlobalBuffer\n5. Copy source data to new buffer using optimized DWORD-aligned copy\n6. Copy remaining bytes (0-3 bytes) using byte-aligned copy\n\nParameters:\npbSourceBuffer: Pointer to source data buffer to copy from\ndwBufferSize: Size in bytes of data to copy to new buffer\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_pGlobalBuffer is NULL initially, skips deallocation step\n- Uses REP MOVSD for efficient 4-byte aligned copying\n- Handles remaining 1-3 bytes with REP MOVSB\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4ac - Ordinal number for buffer deallocation function\n0x4ad - Ordinal number for buffer allocation function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:661ecb5e140955c0a623d2153f720289",
