      "name": "GetAuthenticationSessionId",
      "signature": "uint GetAuthenticationSessionId(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current authentication session identifier for network operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read authentication session ID from global memory location\n2. Return session ID value directly to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nCurrent authentication session identifier (uint)\n- 0x00000000: Session not initialized or reset to default\n- Non-zero: Valid session identifier assigned during authentication process\n\nSpecial Cases:\nSession ID is set to 0 during GenerateAuthenticationCredentials initialization\nand populated with actual values during authentication handshake.",
