      "name": "GetAuthenticationHandle",
      "signature": "HANDLE GetAuthenticationHandle(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieve authentication handle from global string buffer.\n\nThis function accesses a pre-stored authentication handle from the global\nstring buffer at offset 512. Used by authentication subsystem to obtain\nhandle values for packet creation and authentication operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Access global authentication buffer g_abGlobalStringBuffer\n2. Load 4-byte authentication handle from offset 0x200 (512 decimal)\n3. Return handle value directly without validation\n4. Caller receives handle for subsequent authentication operations\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nHANDLE - Authentication handle value stored at g_abGlobalStringBuffer[512]\n        Returns whatever 4-byte value is stored at the buffer offset\n        No validation performed on handle validity\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer is assumed to be properly initialized before function call\nNo bounds checking performed - assumes valid buffer state\nHandle validity determined by initialization code elsewhere\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x200 (512): Fixed offset within g_abGlobalStringBuffer for handle storage\n- g_abGlobalStringBuffer base: 0x6ff399f0 (1024-byte global buffer)  \n- Handle storage address: 0x6ff39bf0 (computed as base + 0x200)\n\nError Handling:\nNo error checking - direct memory access with trust assumption\nCaller must ensure buffer initialization before invoking function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7b4de9f0cf357b113d12e0c7e214792b",
