      "name": "ReleaseDynamicBufferLock",
      "signature": "void ReleaseDynamicBufferLock(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases the critical section lock for the dynamic buffer (index 13).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push critical section index 13 (0xd) onto stack as parameter\n2. Call LeaveCriticalSection via FUN_6ff2c45f to release the lock\n3. Clean up stack and return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis is a paired function with FUN_6ff2b372 (AcquireDynamicBufferLock)\nMust be called after every successful buffer lock acquisition\nCritical section index 13 is hardcoded for dynamic buffer operations\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xd (13) - Fixed critical section index for dynamic buffer synchronization",
