      "comment": "Wrapper function that parses delimited string entries using base 1 conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Prepare parameters for StringToUnsignedLongWithBase call  \n2. Pass buffer pointer, source string, end position pointer, and delimiter\n3. Set base parameter to hardcoded value 0x1\n4. Call StringToUnsignedLongWithBase with 6 parameters for parsing\n5. Return control to caller (void return)\n\nParameters:\nlpszBuffer - Pointer to buffer pointer that gets updated during parsing (char **)\nlpszSourceString - Source string buffer to parse for delimited entries (char *)\nlpszEndPosition - Pointer to end position pointer, updated after parsing (char **)\npdwDelimiter - Pointer to delimiter character for entry separation (uint *)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (wrapper function modifies pointers through parameters)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBase is always 0x1 - this wrapper specifically handles base-1 string parsing\nUsed for parsing gateway lists and configuration entries with delimiters\nBuffer pointers are modified to track parsing progress through parameter references\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 (decimal 1) - Base parameter passed to underlying string conversion function",
