      "name": "ReleaseCriticalSection9",
      "signature": "void ReleaseCriticalSection9(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases critical section index 9 used for allocation synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push constant 9 onto stack as critical section index parameter\n2. Call ReleaseCriticalSectionByIndex(9) to unlock critical section\n3. Clean up stack by popping ECX register\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis function is a lightweight wrapper specifically for critical section 9, which is used to synchronize memory allocation operations in AllocateMemoryWithRetry. The function uses __stdcall calling convention with stack cleanup.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x9 (9): Critical section index for memory allocation synchronization",
