      "name": "WriteToValidatedStream",
      "signature": "int WriteToValidatedStream(uint dwStreamIndex, char * lpszData, uint dwDataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Performs validated write operation to a stream with thread safety\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwStreamIndex is within valid range (< g_dwStreamCount)\n2. Calculate bucket index using dwStreamIndex >> 5 (divide by 32)\n3. Calculate slot index using dwStreamIndex & 0x1f (modulo 32)\n4. Access StreamIO descriptor from g_apStreamDescriptors[bucket][slot]\n5. Check if stream position has active flag (nPosition & 0x1) set\n6. If invalid stream or inactive, set thread error code to 9 and return -1\n7. If valid stream, acquire exclusive lock via FUN_6ff31601\n8. Call actual write operation WriteStreamWithTextConversion with stream data\n9. Release exclusive lock via FUN_6ff31660\n10. Return result from write operation\n\nParameters:\ndwStreamIndex - Stream identifier for bucket/slot lookup (uint)\nlpszData - Pointer to data buffer to write (char *)\ndwDataSize - Size of data to write in bytes (uint)\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: Result from actual write operation (typically bytes written)\nError: -1 when stream invalid or inactive\n\nSpecial Cases:\nStream validation uses two-level indexing: bucket = index/32, slot = index%32\nError code 9 indicates invalid stream index\nError code 0 indicates general failure condition\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1f (31): Bit mask for slot index within bucket (modulo 32)\n0x5 (5): Right shift count for bucket calculation (divide by 32)\n0x1 (1): Active flag bit mask in nPosition field\n0x9 (9): Error code for invalid stream\n0x4 (4): Byte offset to nPosition field in StreamIO structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nStreamIO structure (36 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x00   | 4    | Unknown    | uint | Purpose unknown\n0x04   | 4    | nPosition  | uint | Stream position with flag bits\n...    | ...  | ...        | ...  | Additional fields not accessed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
