      "name": "ReleaseCriticalSectionByAddress",
      "signature": "void ReleaseCriticalSectionByAddress(uint dwAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Release a critical section using either index-based or direct pointer-based approach.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input address is within critical section pool range (0x6ff38ba0 to 0x6ff38e00)\n2. If address is in range: Calculate critical section index using bit shift arithmetic\n3. Add base index offset (0x1c) and call ReleaseCriticalSectionByIndex\n4. If address is outside range: Add structure offset (0x20) to get CRITICAL_SECTION pointer\n5. Call LeaveCriticalSection with calculated pointer\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  dwAddress - Memory address that either points to a critical section pool entry or contains a CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return a value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Pool range check uses exclusive bounds: address must be > 0x6ff38b9f AND < 0x6ff38e01\n  - Index calculation: (address - 0x6ff38ba0) >> 5 converts byte offset to 32-byte aligned index\n  - Direct pointer path assumes CRITICAL_SECTION structure at offset +0x20 from input address\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6ff38ba0 - Start of critical section pool (exclusive lower bound 0x6ff38b9f + 1)\n  0x6ff38e00 - End of critical section pool (exclusive upper bound)\n  0x900c7460 - Negative offset constant (-0x6ff38ba0) for pool-relative calculation\n  0x5 - Right shift by 5 bits (divide by 32) for index calculation\n  0x1c - Base index offset (28 decimal) added to calculated pool index\n  0x20 - Byte offset to CRITICAL_SECTION structure within containing object",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
