      "name": "ReleaseCriticalSectionConditional",
      "signature": "void ReleaseCriticalSectionConditional(int nIndex, CriticalSectionContainer * pCriticalSectionContainer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Conditionally releases a critical section based on index value using different release mechanisms.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load critical section index parameter from stack\n2. Compare index value against threshold 0x14 (20 decimal)\n3. Branch to indexed release if index < 20, otherwise use direct release\n4. For indexed release: Add offset 0x1c to index and call ReleaseCriticalSectionByIndex\n5. For direct release: Calculate critical section address and call LeaveCriticalSection\n6. Return to caller without return value\n\nParameters:\n- nIndex (int): Critical section index value for selection between release mechanisms\n- pCriticalSectionContainer (CriticalSectionContainer*): Pointer to container structure holding critical section data\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function performs synchronization release without return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Index boundary at 0x14 determines release mechanism selection\n- Indexed path uses ReleaseCriticalSectionByIndex with calculated offset\n- Direct path uses LeaveCriticalSection with structure member access\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x14 (20): Maximum index threshold for indexed critical section release\n- 0x1c (28): Offset value added to index for ReleaseCriticalSectionByIndex call\n- 0x20 (32): Byte offset from container base to criticalSection member\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type                   | Description\n-------|------|------------------|------------------------|---------------------------\n0x00   | 32   | dwReserved1-8    | uint[8]               | Reserved container fields\n0x20   | 24   | criticalSection  | _RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION | Windows critical section",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
