      "name": "FreeSourceBuffer",
      "signature": "void FreeSourceBuffer(RectFArray * pRectF)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Frees the internal buffer of a RectFArray structure.\n\nThis function is part of the RectF cleanup pathway, called during\nregion destruction. It handles deallocation of the dynamically\nallocated rectangle buffer stored at offset +8 in the structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load buffer pointer from pRectF->pBuffer (offset +8)\n2. Test if buffer pointer is NULL\n3. If non-NULL, call SMemFree to deallocate the buffer\n4. Return (no cleanup of structure itself)\n\nParameters:\n- pRectF (RectFArray*): Pointer to RectFArray structure to clean up\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
      "method": "MNE",
